{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>חושך, גם</b> — two joined [words]. He informs that the trait of silence is good, that is, one who withholds his words and is silent — [this] is their knowledge, and רוח is the knowledge, meaning that his knowledge is precious. And the opposite of this: כל רוחו יוציא כסיל." "<b>וגם</b> — to include beyond one who withholds his words: גם אויל מחריש חכם יחשב."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The bracketed text and the phrase 'ורוח הוא הדעת' appear garbled in the source; translated hyper-literally as the witnesses stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:26.321642957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}